<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch PTT workers to get three pct pay rise.</title>
<headline>Dutch PTT workers to get three pct pay rise.</headline>
<dateline>THE HAGUE 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Post and telecoms group PTT Nederland NV said it had reached an agreement with labour unions which would give 92,000 of its workers in the Netherlands two pay rises of three percent on April 1, 1997 and April 1, 1998.</p>
<p>The two-year deal, which still has to be approved by union members, also allows PTT Nederland subsidiaries to make separate arrangements on payment for work outside normal working hours.</p>
<p>The company said this would result in greater flexibility and reduced costs for the subsidiaries in question.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
